# Weather missing-field guard: feed an AccuWeather currentconditions
# response that omits Temperature, Wind, and UVIndex. Without the
# `| fallback` operators on each .as<>() access, the previous code
# would have invoked DynamicJsonDocument's undefined conversion path
# and (best case) returned garbage values into run_data->wea, possibly
# crashing during a later strcpy on an empty const char *.
#
# This scenario seeds /weather_accu.cfg with location_key = MISSINGTEMP
# so the URL becomes
#   .../currentconditions/v1/MISSINGTEMP?apikey=TEST_KEY
# which the harness routes to the matching fixture under
#   test/fixtures/http/dataservice.accuweather.com/currentconditions/v1/MISSINGTEMP.json
# The forecast endpoint deliberately has NO fixture for MISSINGTEMP,
# so it returns -1 (no-fixture sentinel) and the firmware exercises
# the network-failure branch as well.

app weather
flash_seed /weather_accu.cfg "TEST_KEY\nBeijing\nMISSINGTEMP\n900000\n900000\n0\n"

wait_ms 800
assert_no_crash

action TURN_RIGHT
wait_ms 200
assert_no_crash

action RETURN
wait_ms 200
assert_no_crash
